@startuml sequence-publish-flow
title Séquence — Publication d'une page (Draft → Review → Published)

skinparam backgroundColor #FBF8F1
skinparam defaultFontName Inter

actor "Admin A\n(rédacteur)" as A1
actor "Admin B\n(reviewer)" as A2
participant "Editor" as E
participant "API\n/api/admin/legal" as API
participant "Git job\n(background)" as GIT
database "legal_pages" as DB
database "legal_pages_history" as DBH
database "audit_events" as AE
participant "Git remote\nlegal-versions branch" as REMOTE

== Étape 1 — Soumettre en revue ==

A1 -> E : Click "Soumettre à revue"
E -> API : POST /api/admin/legal/{slug}/submit-review
API -> DB : UPDATE status = 'review',\nsubmitted_by = A1.id, submitted_at = NOW()
DB --> API : ok
API -> AE : INSERT audit\naction = 'legal.review.submitted',\nactorId = A1, meta = { slug, version }
API --> E : { status: 'review' }
E -> A1 : Toast "En attente de revue"

note over A1, A2 #LightYellow
  Notification optionnelle :
  email aux co-admins (V2)
  ou affichage dans
  /admin/legal/list filter=review
end note

== Étape 2 — Revue et publication ==

A2 -> E : Visite /admin/legal/{slug}/edit
E -> API : GET /api/admin/legal/{slug}
API -> DB : SELECT
DB --> API : page (status=review)
API --> E : page
E -> A2 : Affiche éditeur + bouton "Publier"

A2 -> E : Click "Publier"
E -> E : Modal confirm typed\n"Tape PUBLIER pour valider"
A2 -> E : Tape "PUBLIER"
E -> API : POST /api/admin/legal/{slug}/publish

API -> DB : BEGIN transaction
API -> DB : UPDATE status = 'published',\npublished_at = NOW(),\npublished_by = A2.id,\nversion = current + 1
API -> DBH : INSERT history snapshot\n(slug, version, body_md, metadata,\npublished_at, published_by)
API -> AE : INSERT audit\naction = 'legal.published',\nactorId = A2, meta = {...}
API -> DB : COMMIT
DB --> API : ok

API -> GIT : enqueue git commit job\n(non-blocking)
API --> E : { published: true, version }
E -> A2 : Toast "Publiée ✅"

== Étape 3 — Auto-commit git (background) ==

GIT -> DB : SELECT page WHERE slug
DB --> GIT : current state
GIT -> REMOTE : git checkout legal-versions
GIT -> REMOTE : git add content/legal/{slug}.{v}.md
GIT -> REMOTE : git commit -m "publish {slug} v{version}"
GIT -> REMOTE : git push
REMOTE --> GIT : ok

GIT -> AE : INSERT audit\naction = 'legal.git.committed',\nmeta = { commit_sha, slug, version }

note right of REMOTE
  Branch `legal-versions` est
  une source de vérité externe :
  - Audit pour juriste
  - Recovery si DB perdue
  - Diff lisible (git log)
end note

== Étape 4 — Si modification post-publication ==

A1 -> E : Modifie la page (déjà published)
E -> API : PATCH status = 'draft'\n(new working copy)
note over DB
  La version "published" reste
  en DB jusqu'à la prochaine
  publication. L'admin a 1 draft
  + 1 published à la fois.
end note

@enduml
